    <expires>2025-09-09T18:00:00+02:00</expires>
    <senderName>LU</senderName>
    <headline>Floods in the south of Luxembourg</headline>
    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;The south of Luxembourg has been placed under awareness level red floods from 08.09.2025 23:00 to 09.09.2025 18:00. The awareness level can be adapted or extended depending on the evolution of the situation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;The continuous rainfall during the night, combined with localized heavy precipitations over short periods, is currently causing a very rapid rise in water levels, particularly in the south and center of the country. The main areas of concern are currently along the Alzette as well as the White and Black Ernz rivers. The development of watercourses will largely depend on the actual localized heavy rainfall.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;Forecasts remain uncertain. In the affected areas, there is a significant risk of widespread flooding. For all seasonal activities near watercourses (such as campsites, construction sites, etc.), extreme caution is advised.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please take precautions and inform yourself on the right behaviour to adopt.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For further information, measured and forecasted water levels, please visit the &amp;#39;inondations.lu&amp;#39; website and follow attentively the information provided in the flood reports.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    <parameter>
